  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">M23 Crisis Response in North Kivu 2 (extension DRCC64)- DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve, by March 2025,  the socio -sanitary conditions of the populations affected by the crisis by ensuring:  - Access to potable water in Internally Displaced Person (IDP) sites, returnee zones, host communities and health centers;  - Access to adequate, dignified and hygienic sanitation facilities and,  - ensuring a systematic approach to encourage the widespread adoption of safe hygiene practices to keep people and their environment clean through the promotion of hygiene knowledge and practices and community engagement;  - responding to emergency food needs, the acquisition of essential household items, and primary health care coverage by organizing &quot;multi -purpose cash distributions&quot; (food, essential household items, and health);  - Contributing to the adoption of better community protection practices, reducing the risk of violence and abuse, particularly for women, girls, and disproportionately affected groups in the intervention area. This project will be implemented directly in the localities of Kanyaruchinya, Rusaya (Nyiragongo territory), Lushagala extension site (in Goma town), Bweremana, Sake, Kitshanga and Mweso (in Masisi territory) with the collaboration of the central office of the health zones of KIROTSHE, Mweso, Goma &amp; Nyiragongo and the local communities as well as MINOVA in South Kivu. An estimated number of 15920 Households have been targeted for this project</narrative>
  </description>
